00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:35.880
Instead, you set the
onboarding behavior centrally

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:40.110
in the environment setting
and monitoring configuration,

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:43.860
and Defender for Cloud
applies it consistently

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.600
across the selected scope.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.920
Now, let's shift from Azure-only
to hybrid and multi-cloud.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:56.580
If you run servers
on-premise, in other cloud,

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:01.110
or in a mixed environment,
you still want a single place

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:04.500
to understand risk and
respond to threat.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.000
And that's exactly what
connecting to non-Azure assets

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.300
to Defender for Cloud enables.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:15.750
In this module, we will
focus on three outcomes:

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:20.580
connecting a non-Azure machine
to Microsoft Defender for Cloud,

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.740
connecting an AWS account,
